    "latest_update": "R-137 proves the exact chronologically typed direct/future split of the finite R-136 raw telescope and an executable nonzero future-column fixture. It identifies only the future six-row current with the two R-079 connection channels, keeps every other signed-owner companion separate, reuses the R-084 derivative-free OU norm without reclaiming it, and records why bounded multipliers and bookkeeping direct sums do not supply the missing spatial exponent or physical cross-k orthogonality. The adversarial audit repairs the draft filtration witness, the insertion/reveal typing, Sobolev quantifiers, smooth-cylinder derivatives, future-shell geometry, and the R-135 applicability boundary. The production owner, both spatial branches, once-owned ledger, positive headroom, low and matching data, strict gap, absolute anchor, and both A13 gates remain open.",
    "success_condition": "Prove A13-CLASSII-COMPLETE-RAW-DOOB-DIRECT-FUTURE-SPATIAL-ONE-USE-BOUND. Instantiate the t(k)<=r and t(k)>r split in every complete R-123/R-125 owner, including low, recombined visits, exhaustive output clusters, both R-079 current channels, all six rows, trace, rational, 2680/729 Cartan, R-063 forest, and common heat exactly once. Prove the R-087-type projected spatial estimate for the direct triangle. For the future triangle, either prove an R-135-compatible unique last-insertion transpose with m>=k+5 or a direct integrated signed substitute. Prove one deterministic nonnegative sum_k q_k<=Q without owner, reveal, visit, cluster, row, or refinement multiplicity. Use R-135 only in the compatible transposed branch, certify positive near/balanced headroom at one finite collar, prove complete low and matching data, strict gap, and absolute anchor, apply R-129 once, and only then continue through R-093 toward OVERLAP_src and Nelson. Removals, interacting-measure construction, and Sector A remain open."
